From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] build: allow packagers to retain debug symbols until install

The unconditional post-build strip removes all debug information before RPM
can extract its debuginfo package. Keep upstream's default standalone behavior
but allow distribution builds to defer stripping to their packaging tools.
No source, optimization, feature, or test is removed.

SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -387,7 +387,8 @@
 # ==============================================================================
 # Strip debug symbols on Linux only.
 # Excluded on macOS: stripping before code signing invalidates the signature.
-if (UNIX AND NOT APPLE)
+option(GARLIC_STRIP_BINARY "Strip the standalone binary after building" ON)
+if (UNIX AND NOT APPLE AND GARLIC_STRIP_BINARY)
     add_custom_command(
         TARGET GarlicGUI POST_BUILD
         COMMAND strip $<TARGET_FILE:GarlicGUI>
